      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for those. they're a good start, but i think we can make the contrast way sharper to really land the satire. specifically, i want the \"local\" character to feel a bit more raw and gritty, maybe using more street slang or sounding a little more uneducated/aggressive compared to the condo resident. and for the new resident, can you make them sound even more \"pseudo-intellectual\" or performatively progressive? i want the reader to immediately feel the class difference through how they talk and the way they view the people around them.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
